WEBVTT

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.395
A gate can stop a bad route.

00:00:06.455 --> 00:00:10.483
But a robot that only ever hears no, never
arrives.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:15.177
On forty test buildings, the model gave a
usable route twice.

00:00:16.927 --> 00:00:19.942
So this project goes one step further.

00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:23.132
When the model is wrong, it finds the
right route.

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:26.031
And when there is no right route, it
stops.

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:34.436
The model proposes. The verifier refuses.

00:00:38.386 --> 00:00:42.058
The same start and goal go to a classical
planner,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.915
on the fine map the model never saw.

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:48.461
It plans with a wider berth than the check
demands.

00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:52.079
Twenty centimetres, where ten and a half
would do.

00:00:52.139 --> 00:00:56.688
Then the new route is verified as well,
before anything moves.

00:00:58.637 --> 00:01:03.938
One more trap. A route can be perfectly
safe, and go to the wrong place.

00:01:03.998 --> 00:01:07.915
So the gate asks for both. Safe, and at
the goal.

00:01:09.865 --> 00:01:15.549
Forty proposals. Two forwarded untouched.
Thirty five recovered from unsafe.

00:01:15.499 --> 00:01:18.987
Three recovered from the wrong
destination.

00:01:19.046 --> 00:01:22.887
Unsafe recoveries sent to the motors:
zero.

00:01:28.237 --> 00:01:30.765
Now, wall the goal off completely.

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:35.014
There is no safe route. The only right
answer is to stop.

00:01:36.964 --> 00:01:41.586
The planner searches everywhere it can
reach, and finds no way in.

00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:45.194
So the shield halts. It does not invent a
route.

00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:47.974
Ten sealed goals. Ten halts.

00:01:53.125 --> 00:01:58.593
All of that was on tidy, generated maps.
Real maps are not tidy.

00:01:58.653 --> 00:02:03.251
So the shield was replayed on three public
sensor recordings.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:08.804
From a single scan, more than half the map
is unknown.

00:02:08.864 --> 00:02:12.896
There, the model gave a usable route once
in forty.

00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:21.010
A map built twenty five milliseconds late
changed three decisions out of seventy
nine.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:25.168
The shield is only as right as the map it
is handed.

00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:31.773
And maps move. When the robot's position
estimate was corrected,

00:02:31.723 --> 00:02:35.838
five of twenty six verified routes stopped
verifying.

00:02:35.899 --> 00:02:39.430
So a route already in flight can be
checked again.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.186
Twenty one kept going. Five stopped.

00:02:47.336 --> 00:02:49.188
Now, the fine print.

00:02:49.248 --> 00:02:51.921
The zero is a guard, not a discovery.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:56.353
The wide berth makes recovered routes pass
by construction.

00:02:56.413 --> 00:03:00.600
The second check is the same rule, applied
more finely.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.965
This is one small model, on forty
buildings.

00:03:03.915 --> 00:03:09.023
And no recording is closed loop. No robot
ever reacted to a halt.

00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:13.067
LLM Nav Shield.

00:03:13.127 --> 00:03:15.704
Detect. Recover. Or halt.
